Everything under this directory comes from the World Development Indicators
(WDI) of the World Bank, from the bulk zips at
https://databank.worldbank.org/data/download/WDI_CSV.zip and
https://datacatalogfiles.worldbank.org/ddh-published/0037712/DR0095335/
(WDI_CSV_YYYY_MM_DD.zip). raw/<release>/MANIFEST.json records each zip's
URL, size, sha256, Last-Modified and ETag.

The World Bank licenses its datasets under CC BY 4.0, and all users agree
to mandatory terms added to it: disputes go to mediation under the WIPO
Mediation Rules and, if not settled within 45 days, to arbitration under
the UNCITRAL Arbitration Rules at the World Bank's headquarters in
Washington, DC (https://datacatalog.worldbank.org/public-licenses, read on
2026-10-02).

Attribution, in the World Bank's format: The World Bank: World Development
Indicators: <the indicator's source, given in series.parquet, column
Source>. The World Bank does not endorse this copy.

Three indicators are under CC BY 3.0 IGO, as their License Type says
(GD_WBL_OVL_ENF, GD_WBL_OVL_LAW, GD_WBL_OVL_SFR).

What was changed:

  - 74 indicators were left out of every release, with all their values,
    metadata rows and footnotes: those that any release labels with a
    licence other than CC BY-4.0 or CC BY 3.0 IGO, or with none (SIPRI,
    IEA, WDPA and other providers' terms, CC BY-NC 4.0, no licence given).
    parquet/<release>/excluded.json lists them with the labels behind
    each.
  - csv/<release>/WDI_CSV_redistributable.zip holds the six CSVs of the
    World Bank's zip without the records of those indicators; every record
    kept is the World Bank's text byte for byte.
  - parquet/<release>/data.parquet holds the values of WDICSV.csv in long
    format (country_code, indicator_code, year, value); empty cells are not
    rows. The other Parquet files are the other CSVs, every column as text,
    with year_int added to footnotes and series_time.
  - no value was changed.

The World Bank's own zips are not included: they contain the indicators
left out.

The code that fetches, checks and converts is MIT, in
https://github.com/yuiseki/wdi-to-parquet, and does not apply here.
